THOUGHT: Marking getColor() as @Nullable removed the original RETURN_NULLABLE error but introduced a new dereference error where getColor() is used without a null check (setAlpha). To reduce the total error count by one, I need to make that usage null-safe, e.g., by returning early if color is null before dereferencing. I’ll update setAlpha to check getColor() for null and return if it is, which preserves behavior (no color means nothing to update) and should eliminate the new error without affecting others.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '40,47c\  public void setAlpha(int ambientAlpha) {
    final Color current = this.getColor();
    if (current == null) {
      return;
    }

    this.setColor(
        new Color(
            current.getRed(),
            current.getGreen(),
            current.getBlue(),
            MathUtilities.clamp(ambientAlpha, 0, 255)));
    this.updateSection(this.environment.getMap().getBounds());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/ColorLayer.java
```

